WEBVTT

00:01.569 --> 00:04.900
Now that we are all here,
let me ask once again.

00:05.420 --> 00:09.650
Albert, did the Holy Church
recognize Van as a Hero?

00:10.090 --> 00:10.740
Yes.

00:11.130 --> 00:13.330
Cardinal Lub has been appointed
as his guardian,

00:13.330 --> 00:15.660
and his blessing has been authenticated.

00:15.660 --> 00:19.180
It seems that from now on he will
work as a Hero of the church.

00:19.690 --> 00:21.670
Hero of the Church...

00:21.950 --> 00:22.790
Red?

00:23.480 --> 00:26.910
Since the church recognized him as a Hero,

00:27.600 --> 00:30.890
I was wondering why he didn't
make a move until now.

00:30.890 --> 00:31.930
You're right.

00:32.320 --> 00:33.810
Speaking of church,

00:33.810 --> 00:37.240
I once visited one at the Great Holy Fortress
of the Last Wall a long time ago.

00:37.240 --> 00:39.420
That's when I met Theodora.

00:39.800 --> 00:40.690
It feels nostalgic.

00:40.950 --> 00:43.740
That was before I joined the party, right?

00:43.740 --> 00:47.570
Did the church know about
Van's existence back then?

00:48.060 --> 00:51.480
If they had known that
there were two Heroes,

00:51.480 --> 00:53.720
they would have reacted in some way.

00:54.760 --> 00:56.450
But nothing happened.

00:56.960 --> 00:59.710
It's natural to assume
that they didn't know, but...

01:03.360 --> 01:06.460
Well, I don't blame you
for thinking that way.

01:06.460 --> 01:11.160
The problem is that Van
is coming to Zoltan, right?

01:26.150 --> 01:32.910
BANISHED FROM THE HERO’S PARTY, I DECIDED TO
LIVE A QUIET LIFE IN THE COUNTRYSIDE SEASON 2

02:44.000 --> 02:44.520
#6 LONG VACATION

02:44.520 --> 02:48.020
#6 LONG VACATION
How much does the church know about Ruti?

02:48.440 --> 02:50.390
As far as I know, they know nothing.

02:50.870 --> 02:55.380
Because originally, they didn't talk
too much about the heroes.

02:56.100 --> 02:58.810
Well, it was meant to be.

02:59.280 --> 03:01.800
But thanks to Ruti, who defeated
two demons, and Theodora,

03:01.800 --> 03:03.900
who defeated one
of the Four Demon Kings,

03:03.900 --> 03:06.690
the battle with the Demon King's
army is now at a stalemate.

03:07.110 --> 03:10.290
It is safe to say that the continent
is in a constant state of stability.

03:11.020 --> 03:14.590
The absence of Ruti should not
be a major problem,

03:15.620 --> 03:19.800
but the arrival of a new Hero
is a different story.

03:20.330 --> 03:23.740
If it were known that Ruti, who is supposed
to be a Hero, had stopped fighting,

03:23.740 --> 03:25.360
he would not remain silent.

03:26.690 --> 03:29.450
Is there any way to avoid
running into him?

03:29.450 --> 03:30.820
How about putting on a disguise?

03:31.300 --> 03:33.170
They would probably recognize her.

03:33.170 --> 03:35.280
Because Ms. Ruti is very conspicuous.

03:35.280 --> 03:36.320
Yeah...

03:36.760 --> 03:41.540
Van's goal is to get the previous
Demon King's airship, right?

03:41.910 --> 03:47.220
Then, how about you guys leave
Zoltan for a while until then?

03:47.220 --> 03:48.280
Huh?

03:48.280 --> 03:51.070
How about a little sightseeing?

03:51.520 --> 03:54.210
You can leave the herb farm to me.

03:54.210 --> 03:57.930
And I can handle your store!
You should relax.

03:57.930 --> 03:59.760
Well, I'll let you do that.

04:00.240 --> 04:01.110
Yep.

04:01.110 --> 04:03.260
I'll be your liaison.

04:03.690 --> 04:06.230
I'm staying in Zoltan, just in case.

04:06.570 --> 04:09.000
Wouldn't it be bad if you met
with the Cardinal?

04:09.000 --> 04:11.080
Of course, I don't intend to meet him.

04:11.080 --> 04:14.200
But I have a bad feeling about this.

04:15.340 --> 04:16.870
And if I do meet him,

04:16.870 --> 04:20.950
there's a reason I can tell him
I was banished

04:22.280 --> 04:24.160
from the party of heroes!

04:24.720 --> 04:28.410
Danan is stronger now than he
was when he had his right arm.

04:31.840 --> 04:32.530
I agree.

04:32.530 --> 04:32.980
Really?!

04:32.980 --> 04:33.680
I think so too.

04:33.680 --> 04:34.800
Really?!

04:39.720 --> 04:42.010
It's a peaceful place.

04:42.810 --> 04:44.510
The village of St. Durant.

04:44.510 --> 04:47.920
Durant is the name of the hero
who saved this village.

04:48.340 --> 04:51.260
So he's a hero who fought
in the war here?

04:51.650 --> 04:54.980
No, he was a lumberjack
who was proud of his strength.

04:54.980 --> 04:56.030
A lumberjack?

04:56.780 --> 04:58.400
He saved the settlers

04:58.710 --> 05:01.120
who lost everything
in the Hill Giant's attack

05:01.120 --> 05:05.400
by building houses for all
the villagers in one night.

05:05.400 --> 05:08.020
Oh, really?

05:12.220 --> 05:14.360
So this is hero Durant!

05:15.050 --> 05:16.500
Hero Durant.

05:16.950 --> 05:20.960
There are many heroes who slaughter
a hundred enemies in one night,

05:20.960 --> 05:24.630
and there is only one hero who builds
a house for a hundred people to live in.

05:25.050 --> 05:27.140
He falls and carries a great tree away.

05:27.140 --> 05:30.060
Behold his beautiful pectoral muscles.

05:32.330 --> 05:36.380
Come to think of it, we've never
been to a tourist place like this.

05:36.380 --> 05:37.400
I'm so excited.

05:41.650 --> 05:44.460
Wow, this stuff is interesting.

05:44.460 --> 05:47.500
It looks like nobles and
merchants visit often,

05:47.500 --> 05:49.620
so maybe all kinds of things gather here.

05:49.620 --> 05:52.470
The ones around there
are just ornamental.

05:52.470 --> 05:53.240
Erm...

05:54.120 --> 05:55.400
Do you want to buy something?

05:55.400 --> 05:56.320
Yes!

05:58.150 --> 06:00.970
This is your key.

06:00.970 --> 06:01.880
Thanks.

06:02.480 --> 06:04.740
Well, then, enjoy your stay.

06:04.740 --> 06:06.040
Let's get in.

06:06.040 --> 06:06.890
Okay.

06:09.000 --> 06:10.720
Woah!

06:10.720 --> 06:12.470
It's pretty good!

06:12.470 --> 06:13.860
The ambience is nice.

06:24.120 --> 06:27.380
Is Ms. Ruti already there?

06:28.670 --> 06:32.750
Once this thing is over,
should we go on a little trip too?

06:41.400 --> 06:42.500
So beautiful.

06:42.500 --> 06:45.650
They must be mixing something.
How interesting.

06:46.070 --> 06:48.920
Why don't we buy some more
of these on our way home?

06:48.920 --> 06:52.370
Good idea. I want to show it
to Tisse and Yarandrala.

06:52.370 --> 06:54.420
Mr. Crawly Wawly will be happy
to see it too.

07:04.880 --> 07:06.950
Hero Van, huh?

07:07.630 --> 07:09.950
He may have arrived there by now.

07:10.580 --> 07:12.760
I hope we can get home soon.

07:13.920 --> 07:17.080
I know the severity of a Hero's impulses.

07:17.530 --> 07:19.960
Even if I wanted to stay longer,

07:20.280 --> 07:22.620
the blessing of the Hero
would not let me do so.

07:27.900 --> 07:30.340
I want to enjoy this time now.

07:33.660 --> 07:34.980
That's right.

07:36.910 --> 07:39.350
Then, let's make honey milk.

07:39.350 --> 07:40.420
Yes!

07:55.400 --> 07:57.750
That was a delicious restaurant.

07:58.180 --> 08:00.900
That strange leaf is making me curious.

08:00.900 --> 08:02.610
That is snakeweed.

08:02.610 --> 08:05.850
Originally, it was used
to settle the stomach.

08:05.850 --> 08:07.920
Maybe we can pick one up around here.

08:10.060 --> 08:10.890
She's in trouble!

08:11.480 --> 08:12.680
Are you okay?

08:12.680 --> 08:13.810
Yes.

08:13.810 --> 08:15.540
It hurts...

08:15.540 --> 08:16.840
Let's get her to the cottage.

08:16.840 --> 08:17.660
Yeah.

08:20.870 --> 08:23.850
Ms. Kate, is this the area that hurts?

08:24.360 --> 08:25.860
Yes.

08:26.430 --> 08:27.980
Is there a doctor in this village?

08:27.980 --> 08:29.500
There is no doctor in this village.

08:29.500 --> 08:30.570
I see.

08:30.970 --> 08:32.740
I'm not a doctor,

08:32.740 --> 08:35.620
but I have knowledge about
injuries and illnesses.

08:36.350 --> 08:38.559
May I ask you questions?

08:38.559 --> 08:39.620
Okay.

08:40.169 --> 08:43.370
Have you noticed anything
unusual recently?

08:43.710 --> 08:45.650
No, not really...

08:45.650 --> 08:49.630
Ah, I cut my foot a few days ago.

08:49.930 --> 08:50.970
Your foot?

08:50.970 --> 08:55.080
Yeah, it was just an accident at work.

08:55.420 --> 08:57.390
How long have you had
numbness in your limbs?

08:57.660 --> 08:58.380
Eh?

08:59.160 --> 09:02.300
I guess a while ago...

09:02.300 --> 09:03.740
What did you find out?

09:04.180 --> 09:07.400
I'm afraid you got poisoned
when you were injured.

09:07.400 --> 09:08.560
What?!

09:08.560 --> 09:10.990
Magic can suppress the pain,

09:10.990 --> 09:13.560
but it can't eliminate the toxins
in your body.

09:17.170 --> 09:18.530
What should I do?

09:19.580 --> 09:22.200
Red, can you make its medicine?

09:23.140 --> 09:26.920
Yes. I'll make a concoction
with the herbs we have.

09:27.340 --> 09:28.660
Is that okay?

09:29.010 --> 09:30.930
Yes! Please do!

09:31.300 --> 09:34.430
With my mixing skills,
it'll take a while.

09:34.430 --> 09:35.180
Ruti,

09:35.610 --> 09:40.190
there's an herb that I'm missing,
so could you go get it for me?

09:40.190 --> 09:42.440
Okay. What should I get?

09:42.440 --> 09:45.190
Snakeweed.
The kind we just ate earlier.

09:45.830 --> 09:49.610
Ask the owner, and I'm sure he'll
tell you where it grows.

09:49.610 --> 09:50.690
As long as I have it,

09:50.690 --> 09:54.600
I can make a potion with the same effect
with the ingredients I have on hand.

09:54.600 --> 09:55.660
I understand.

09:57.280 --> 09:59.410
Rit, please take care
of Ms. Kate's illness.

09:59.870 --> 10:02.370
Use magic to ease her pain
as much as possible.

10:02.700 --> 10:03.290
Okay.

10:34.870 --> 10:36.700
Welcome back, Ruti.
Wait...

10:37.490 --> 10:38.650
What happened with you?

10:39.000 --> 10:41.200
I just fell down a ravine.

10:42.440 --> 10:44.150
Big brother, here.

10:44.150 --> 10:45.580
Thank you, Ruti.

10:46.150 --> 10:48.040
This will complete my medicine.

10:51.410 --> 10:53.300
Then, I'll go get someone.

11:09.000 --> 11:12.860
You should be fine now, but please
take your meds for a while.

11:13.240 --> 11:15.900
Thank you so much for your help!

11:19.450 --> 11:20.360
Eh?

11:20.360 --> 11:21.120
Huh?

11:21.680 --> 11:23.540
Why are there so many people here?!

11:24.110 --> 11:27.420
I couldn't find Ms. Kate's house,
so I was asking around,

11:27.420 --> 11:28.880
and they all came.

11:29.230 --> 11:31.520
So you took care of Kate, right?

11:31.520 --> 11:35.350
This is the village's secret recipe!
You should try it!

11:35.350 --> 11:36.560
Here, take this too!

11:36.560 --> 11:37.890
Take it!

11:37.890 --> 11:40.040
Oh, come on, don't be shy.

11:40.040 --> 11:42.410
Ah... Thank you very much...

11:47.150 --> 11:48.770
I'm beat...

11:49.460 --> 11:51.290
How's Red's condition?

12:07.610 --> 12:08.760
It's done.

12:08.760 --> 12:10.170
Yaay!

12:11.390 --> 12:13.720
So, what is this dinner you've made?

12:13.720 --> 12:15.830
It's a dish called curry.

12:15.830 --> 12:18.790
It's a local dish from Durant's hometown.

12:18.790 --> 12:20.670
The recipe you got earlier?

12:20.670 --> 12:22.350
The color is amazing.

12:23.660 --> 12:25.430
The aroma is mouth-watering.

12:25.750 --> 12:26.430
So...

12:26.840 --> 12:29.340
What's with that outfit?

12:29.340 --> 12:31.810
Huh? We're on vacation, right?

12:32.150 --> 12:35.070
And the floor here is so warm.

12:35.650 --> 12:40.460
I've heard there's geothermal heat
around here, so maybe that's the reason.

12:41.400 --> 12:42.070
And...

12:42.710 --> 12:43.960
Ruti?

12:44.460 --> 12:45.630
I forgot my swimsuit.

12:45.630 --> 12:46.760
That's nonsense.

12:50.020 --> 12:51.500
Well, whatever.

12:51.930 --> 12:52.710
Let's eat.

12:52.710 --> 12:53.440
Yeah!

12:58.900 --> 13:02.470
The spiciness really hits the spot,
and it's delicious!

13:02.470 --> 13:05.470
And it goes well with fresh bread.
So yummy.

13:05.880 --> 13:09.550
Still, I haven't heard any news from them.

13:09.940 --> 13:12.400
I wonder if it's okay
to take it easy like this.

13:12.400 --> 13:14.980
If we leave, things will only
get more complicated.

13:15.640 --> 13:17.400
Let's trust everyone and wait.

13:21.160 --> 13:22.090
More, please.

13:30.920 --> 13:31.460
Hey.

13:32.180 --> 13:32.830
Mr. Danan.

13:33.370 --> 13:34.680
How's it going?

13:34.680 --> 13:36.680
They haven't come yet.

13:36.990 --> 13:37.800
I see.

13:39.910 --> 13:41.920
Here, eat this.

13:41.920 --> 13:43.640
Thank you very much!

13:46.100 --> 13:47.660
It looks delicious!

13:47.660 --> 13:49.320
I made it myself.

13:52.620 --> 13:53.690
You made it?

13:54.340 --> 13:55.730
You don't want to eat it?

13:56.710 --> 13:57.560
No...

14:05.190 --> 14:05.660
Ah...

14:06.880 --> 14:07.890
It's surprisingly tasty.

14:07.890 --> 14:08.830
Say what?

14:08.830 --> 14:10.580
Ah, I'm sorry!
I slipped on my tongue!

14:10.870 --> 14:12.200
Albert...

14:13.370 --> 14:16.590
I didn't say it clearly...

14:20.620 --> 14:23.050
You saved my life!
Thank you!

14:26.440 --> 14:28.310
M-Mr. Danan...

14:28.820 --> 14:30.510
I'm looking forward to working with you!

14:30.510 --> 14:31.350
Yes!

14:31.350 --> 14:32.380
Do your best, okay?

14:32.380 --> 14:33.260
Yes!

14:38.070 --> 14:39.820
So this is Zoltan.

14:39.820 --> 14:41.660
We have finally arrived here, Van.

14:41.660 --> 14:42.320
Yep.

14:43.600 --> 14:46.230
I can't believe we embarked
on a ship like that...

14:46.230 --> 14:48.100
What a shabby port...

14:50.380 --> 14:51.750
What's wrong?

14:51.750 --> 14:56.120
No, I just remembered an old buddy
of mine saying the same thing.

14:56.120 --> 14:59.820
Was he a hero, too?
I'd like to meet him!

15:00.420 --> 15:03.010
That's not going to happen.

15:03.380 --> 15:07.580
That's right.
Our goal is to save the world.

15:07.580 --> 15:09.650
We can't take unnecessary detours, can we?

15:10.010 --> 15:11.380
That's right.

15:14.620 --> 15:16.270
So that's Hero Van?

15:17.100 --> 15:19.180
He's nothing like Ms. Ruti.

15:24.770 --> 15:26.700
You got a guide yet?

15:27.970 --> 15:30.160
He must have found some lucrative deal

15:30.160 --> 15:32.570
and died in a ditch somewhere.

15:32.570 --> 15:36.220
Only the guide knows
the exact location, right?

15:36.220 --> 15:38.670
Why don't we search alone?

15:38.990 --> 15:40.620
The sun will be setting soon.

15:40.620 --> 15:43.970
Let's talk about our plans
after we get to the inn.

15:49.420 --> 15:50.430
It's done.

15:50.700 --> 15:51.930
Amazing!

15:52.430 --> 15:54.070
That's the Wyvern master for you!

15:55.540 --> 15:56.810
My friend is here.

15:56.810 --> 15:57.670
Your friend?

16:01.550 --> 16:03.650
So it's Mr. Crawly Wawly.

16:03.650 --> 16:05.610
He's a high-spec spider.

16:06.140 --> 16:07.700
As expected of Mr. Crawly Wawly.

16:08.120 --> 16:10.250
It seems that the Hero Van has arrived.

16:10.770 --> 16:13.080
There's been no problem so far.

16:13.080 --> 16:13.920
I see.

16:16.740 --> 16:19.800
Huh? Mr. Crawly Wawly, do you also
do the Wyvern Race?

16:21.500 --> 16:24.000
You really are a high-spec spider,
aren't you?

16:33.100 --> 16:34.720
My name is Tisse.

16:34.720 --> 16:36.930
I'm an assassin who belongs
to the Assassins Guild,

16:36.930 --> 16:39.150
and today I'm acting as a maid.

16:39.150 --> 16:41.400
Thank you very much for coming.

16:41.400 --> 16:45.400
I am Mayor Tornado.
It's an honor to meet you.

16:48.660 --> 16:50.410
Umm...

16:50.840 --> 16:54.260
I'm sorry, but it seems the Hero
is tired from the boat trip.

16:54.260 --> 16:57.420
Ah, of course. I apologize.

16:57.420 --> 16:59.150
Let's meet again later.

17:00.990 --> 17:03.870
Van, I don't like your attitude right now.

17:04.690 --> 17:07.940
I have an idea about the airship.

17:07.940 --> 17:09.380
Get yourself in a good mood.

17:10.380 --> 17:12.589
Mr. Hero, this is the chef's special—

17:12.589 --> 17:14.849
A Hero does not need to eat!

17:16.980 --> 17:18.650
I-I am terribly sorry!

17:26.220 --> 17:27.530
Let's talk outside.

17:27.839 --> 17:32.030
That's a good idea! I've been wanting
to get out of here too!

17:40.390 --> 17:42.790
I'm not asking you to be sociable,

17:42.790 --> 17:46.170
but could you at least make an effort
to hide your grumpiness?

17:46.530 --> 17:48.170
It's the usual question you always ask!

17:48.660 --> 17:51.930
Do you really enjoy
having me nitpick so much?

17:52.390 --> 17:53.820
Of course, I do.

17:53.820 --> 17:56.140
For me, an inexperienced Hero,

17:56.140 --> 17:59.680
I learn a lot from talking with Ms. Esther,
who has a high level of blessing!

18:00.090 --> 18:03.970
Did that ever make him change his mind?

18:04.830 --> 18:07.350
Respect people's feelings more.

18:07.350 --> 18:10.110
They held a party to celebrate

18:10.110 --> 18:11.700
your arrival as a Hero, you know?

18:13.430 --> 18:15.450
Why would they do that?

18:15.820 --> 18:16.920
"Why," you ask?

18:17.390 --> 18:20.850
Is it strange to express their
admiration and gratitude

18:20.850 --> 18:22.460
for the Hero?

18:22.900 --> 18:27.070
Heroes saved people because
God decreed it to be so.

18:27.580 --> 18:30.080
There is no need for admiration
or gratitude.

18:30.740 --> 18:34.450
What is true for you is not true for others.

18:34.860 --> 18:39.540
Besides, a Hero is supposed to give people
the courage to stand up against evil.

18:39.940 --> 18:43.640
It is important to understand
and respect people's hearts,

18:43.640 --> 18:45.340
because there are times when we have

18:45.340 --> 18:47.730
to lead them into battle.

18:48.570 --> 18:52.940
Indeed, it is one of the roles of a Hero
to give people the courage to fight.

18:53.590 --> 18:56.740
When a hero appears, people must be
courageous enough...

18:57.340 --> 18:58.800
...to fight and die.

19:01.180 --> 19:01.900
What?

19:02.930 --> 19:05.010
It is natural to fight bravely

19:05.010 --> 19:09.200
and die as a result because
God demanded so.

19:09.940 --> 19:12.300
There should be no gratitude
or longing there,

19:12.300 --> 19:14.890
but only faith in the Lord Demis.

19:16.910 --> 19:18.380
You...

19:18.920 --> 19:21.680
Are you asking those who fight with you...

19:22.080 --> 19:23.430
...to die?

19:24.450 --> 19:26.680
You have no feelings for them?

19:27.330 --> 19:29.900
Yes. Martyrdom is faith.

19:30.280 --> 19:31.780
Emotion is impurity.

19:32.280 --> 19:34.740
As expected of Van!
So cool!

19:37.060 --> 19:39.950
We'll be leaving tomorrow.

19:41.100 --> 19:43.430
We will let the Zoltanian
explore the airship.

19:43.860 --> 19:48.010
In the meantime,
we will do what we can.

19:48.010 --> 19:49.460
What do you mean?

19:49.860 --> 19:54.390
We have to go back a bit, but here is
an island where Salt Dragon live.

19:54.390 --> 19:56.430
We have to eliminate it.

19:56.790 --> 19:58.200
Salt Dragon?

19:58.200 --> 20:00.740
It is the dragon of stagnation
and destruction.

20:00.740 --> 20:02.810
In other words, the enemy of the Hero!

20:03.180 --> 20:06.580
Salt Dragon don't attack people
unless they get close.

20:06.580 --> 20:08.890
It should have no major effects on people.

20:09.310 --> 20:11.690
Are you sure we should take down
such an opponent?

20:12.000 --> 20:15.850
It is a good opponent to raise
the level of Van's blessing.

20:15.850 --> 20:17.800
Besides, according to the information,

20:17.800 --> 20:22.660
there is a treasure of the Fairy King
that was stolen by the Salt Dragon.

20:22.660 --> 20:24.530
It would be worthwhile to get it.

20:24.530 --> 20:25.220
But...

20:25.220 --> 20:26.370
Don't worry!

20:26.370 --> 20:29.740
It is right to get the treasure
by defeating monsters.

20:29.740 --> 20:32.100
It is written so in the
scriptures of the church.

20:32.580 --> 20:36.470
If you make enemies unnecessarily,
you will regret it.

20:36.900 --> 20:39.470
Because it is the Hero who destroys all evil.

20:39.940 --> 20:43.400
I am always the enemy
of all evil in the world.

20:45.340 --> 20:48.230
Now, let's get back
before the food gets cold.

20:48.230 --> 20:51.700
I hear that the fish dish
goes well with Zoltan wine.

20:51.700 --> 20:53.150
I am going back to the inn.

20:53.450 --> 20:55.860
Since God made the wine,

20:55.860 --> 20:58.790
it is the duty of the faithful to enjoy it.

21:00.570 --> 21:03.100
Well, it's just my imagination.

21:12.100 --> 21:15.250
You came here to steal our hidden treasure?

21:15.250 --> 21:18.510
Know your place, thieves!

21:22.740 --> 21:23.830
Don't get cheeky!

21:23.830 --> 21:26.990
Go away, you mortals!

21:35.070 --> 21:36.860
I, Van the Hero...

21:36.860 --> 21:38.740
...will banish all evil!

21:59.280 --> 22:00.740
You did it, Van!

22:00.740 --> 22:01.460
Yeah!

22:04.760 --> 22:05.660
That's the shield...

22:06.970 --> 22:08.580
...of the Fairy King!
